WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:05.190
<b>25 Years Ago</b>

3
00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:06.900
[NARRATOR]
This is a tale of
adventure, 25 years in the past.

4
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.620
[NARRATOR]
It begins not long
before the Great Pirate Era

5
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.950
that we know of today.

6
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:49.550
[sighs]

7
00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.510
[chuckles]

8
00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.510
Good ale and blue
skies! What a day!

9
00:00:54.510 --> 00:01:00.560
[Roger Pirates cheering]

10
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.680
It's been a joy traveling
these seas with you.

11
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.230
Thank you, Roger.

12
00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.730
[GOLD ROGER]
Hm? What are you
going on about, ya big dope?

13
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:18.280
Oden, we should be thanking you!
The whole stinking crew!

14
00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.580
[Gold Roger chuckles]

15
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.460
You're drinking too much
again! Dial it back!

16
00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:33.670
Maybe if my doctor wasn't
so drunk, I'd listen to him!

17
00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.470
[both growling]

18
00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:38.760
Well I'm drunk and I'm concerned
about your health, okay?

19
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.470
[Gold Roger groans]
Bastard!

20
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.710
It was a cure for stupidity.

21
00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.040
Ha! You need it, too!

22
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.340
[Gold Roger laughs]

23
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.670
[Crocus groans]

24
00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.800
- [thud]
- [Crocus groans]

25
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:49.960
[GOLD ROGER]
Want some more?

26
00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:02.680
I'm afraid I must return soon.

27
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.720
To the Land of Wano?

28
00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.850
[ODEN]
Yes. There is work left undone.

29
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.360
If it feels like
too much to handle,

30
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.900
you don't have to tackle it
on your own, okay?

31
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.780
[BUGGY]
If you need a hand, Oden,

32
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.900
then this clown will never
let you down! Promise!

33
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.490
[SHANKS]
Yeah, right!
You'll be dead weight!

34
00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.620
Don't kid yourself!

35
00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.080
Hey, how 'bout this?

36
00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.870
I'll come along too
and keep him in check!

37
00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.590
I am grateful. But, no.

38
00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.470
The Kozuki must accomplish
this task alone.

39
00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.970
For the last time,
why is he "Taro" and I'm "Jiro"?

40
00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.960
'Cause only the cool kids
get to be "Taro." [laughs]

41
00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.880
I see. Then It's personal.

42
00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.730
This journey taught me much

43
00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.190
and I'm grateful to
have seen the world.

44
00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.480
I have long questioned why
my country closed its borders.

45
00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.280
I left the Land of Wano
by my own choice,

46
00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.200
so I won't be
so selfish as to ask

47
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.870
that they make me
Shogun when I return.

48
00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.290
But I will fight for my cause
no matter what.

49
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.420
[ODEN]
With the aid of
my faithful retainers,

50
00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.300
doubtless awaiting my return,

51
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.970
I shall open up
the Land of Wano.

52
00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.890
Together, we shall await
the coming of a new world,

53
00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.680
in 20 years!

54
00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.560
[Roger Pirates cheer]

55
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.430
Are you sure you're ready?

56
00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.400
Yeah! We shall not fail, Roger!

57
00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.190
[NARRATOR]
Now, in the
Land of Wano, 25 years later.

58
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.120
<b>25 Years Later</b>

59
00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.240
<b>Act 3</b>
<b>Wano</b>

60
00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.810
[Orochi chuckles]

61
00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:59.770
Our lord is truly blessed.

62
00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:02.650
Even the weather itself
shows him its favor.

63
00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.480
Kyoshiro will look after
the capital and remain here.

64
00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:09.460
[Townspeople cheering]

65
00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.740
You, deliver
the message, quickly.

66
00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.030
[SUBORDINATE A]
Yes, sir!

67
00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.570
Aw, the poor guy!

68
00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.490
He'll be sad he's
gonna miss the party!

69
00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.450
[NARRATOR]
This is Habu Port,
located in Hakumai.

70
00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.750
It is the largest port
in the Land of Wano

71
00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.210
and the most scenic as well.

72
00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:23.920
Maple trees line
its massive wharf,

73
00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:27.380
framing the entrance to the sea
with a splash of colors.

74
00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.550
The red and orange leaves
fluttering through the air

75
00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.140
give a festive sendoff to
the boats as they depart.

76
00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.770
Let's start the party!

77
00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.100
Bring some saké!

78
00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.350
We should drink and
admire the scenery!

79
00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:45.190
Lord Orochi, perhaps wait
till you see Kaido?

80
00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:49.440
He doesn't care!
Y'think he's not drunk, too?

81
00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.200
This is a banquet
with 30,000 guests!

82
00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.200
We're here to have a good time!

83
00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.290
[NARRATOR]
On the night
of the annual Fire Festival,

84
00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.460
the two leaders who
rule the Land of Wano

85
00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:02.210
come together on
the island of Onigashima.

86
00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.000
There they throw
a lavish banquet,

87
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.710
attended by all of Kaido's army

88
00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.590
and all of Orochi's
army as well.

89
00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.390
[Townspeople chattering]

90
00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.600
[Children giggling]

91
00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.480
[GIRL A]
Hey! Hurry up!

92
00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.380
<b>Flower

Capital</b>

93
00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.380
<b>The Day

of the

Fire

Festival</b>

94
00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:51.390
<b>The Designated Port</b>

95
00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.290
[TOWNSPERSON A]
When you need
a break from dancing,

96
00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:56.040
eat up! Drink up!

97
00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:59.040
And when you're done, get out
there and dance some more!

98
00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:00.550
[Children giggling]

99
00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.380
[TOWNSPERSON B]
It's the only
day we're allowed to drink!

100
00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:04.310
You better believe I'm gonna
savor every last drop of this!

101
00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:06.480
Can we go already?
You look fine!

102
00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.600
Wait! My bangs
are just not working.

103
00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:10.770
[sighs]

104
00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.270
Oh my! The sky is
so clear tonight!

105
00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:19.610
We should have a view of
the full moon in just a bit!

106
00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:24.280
[Children laughing]

107
00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:23.110
[Townsperson E giggles]

108
00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:29.890
<b>Tokage
 Port</b>
<b>Hakumai</b>
<b>Wano Country</b>

109
00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:30.090
<b>Kibi</b>

110
00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:30.170
<b>Kuri Flower 
Capital</b>
<b>Udon</b>

111
00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:30.180
<b>Ringo</b>

112
00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:27.360
[NARRATOR]
In the Land of Wano,
each region has

113
00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:30.490
different seasons at
different times of the year.

114
00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:33.120
[Townsperson E giggles]

115
00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:37.690
<b>Tokage
 Port</b>
<b>Hakumai</b>

116
00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:30.640
<b>Wano Country</b>

117
00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:30.420
<b>Kibi</b>

118
00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:30.220
<b>Kuri Flower 
Capital</b>

119
00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:37.680
<b>Udon</b>

120
00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:30.760
<b>Ringo</b>

121
00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:30.510
<b>Flower 
Capital</b>

122
00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:30.550
<b>Kuri</b>

123
00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:30.840
<b>Udon Hakumai</b>

124
00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:30.380
<b>Kibi Flower 
Capital</b>

125
00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:30.470
<b>Kuri Kibi</b>

126
00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:33.580
The weather also varies
tremendously by location.

127
00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.450
Sunny skies in
one region turn to

128
00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:38.080
foreboding clouds in the next.

129
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.380
[NARRATOR]
Thus, the rendezvous
point at Tokage Port

130
00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:45.000
looked quite different
from the capital.

131
00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:11.740
There is nary a single
ship in sight!

132
00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:14.660
There's nary a single
ship in sight!

133
00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:18.160
Our 4,000 warriors
are missing, too!

134
00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.120
[OKIKU]
How could this be?
We conquered Udon!

135
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:28.170
Our men, they left
the labor camp.

136
00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:29.800
So where could they be now?

137
00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.840
Glancing around, there are signs
that the port was attacked!

138
00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:36.260
It appears the cat
couldn't make it in time.

139
00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.320
[KIN'EMON]
The Smail is not responding.

140
00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:48.820
Whatever has happened,
we cannot contact anyone.

141
00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:51.650
[KIN'EMON]
"Twilight on
the day of the Fire Festival,

142
00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:52.510
At twilight on the day
of the Fire Festival,

143
00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.030
[KIN'EMON]
"Twilight on
the day of the Fire Festival,

144
00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:57.100
at Tokage Port"!

145
00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.310
[KIN'EMON]
This is the rendezvous point,

146
00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.110
without a doubt!

147
00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:03.320
Why hasn't anyone come?

148
00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:03.580
Where could they
have disappeared to?

149
00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:05.670
Where could they have
disappeared to?

150
00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:10.630
[KIN'EMON]
Only a day has passed!

151
00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:13.260
What could have befallen them?

152
00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:16.010
[KIN'EMON]
What is going on here?

153
00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:19.400
[Children gasp]

154
00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:19.590
Sir Luffy, where have you gone?

155
00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:22.070
[KIN'EMON]
Sir Luffy, where have you gone?

156
00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:25.390
Sir Hyogoro, please answer me!

157
00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:31.270
[KIN'EMON]
Dogstorm's Musketeers!

158
00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:32.350
Sir Law!

159
00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:35.080
Anyone!

160
00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.170
We are the retainers
of Kozuki Oden!

161
00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:41.150
We've come to settle the past!

162
00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:47.160
[KIN'EMON]
Twenty years ago,
we failed to save our lord,

163
00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:50.430
and because we could not
die by his side that day,

164
00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.180
we offer up our lives now,

165
00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:56.130
in hopes of seeing justice
served at long last!

166
00:09:58.460 --> 00:09:59.460
However, I must profess that
our lives are not enough.

167
00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:02.570
However, I must profess
that our lives are not enough.

168
00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:07.180
The enemy has 30,000 soldiers!
We need help!

169
00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:09.810
I beg you!

170
00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:13.020
Without your aid,
we shall all die in vain!

171
00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:15.760
Please, answer me! Help us...

172
00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.970
[SHUTENMARU]
Kin'emon, stop! Enough!

173
00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.220
[Orochi cackling]

174
00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:23.870
Look! This sky and this sea.

175
00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:25.950
Heaven itself has abandoned us!

176
00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:26.200
We'll find no aid from
any place...from any man!

177
00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:29.910
We'll find no aid from
any place, from any man!

178
00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:34.580
Something terrible must have
happened to our friends!

179
00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:41.750
[Children gasp]

180
00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:43.120
[PERFORMER A]
Watch out, comin' through!

181
00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.340
Don't just stand there,
dance with us!

182
00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:48.380
This is the one time of the year
you get to let loose!

183
00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.800
Everybody start
moving those feet!

184
00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:59.360
[DOGSTORM]
There's a small
boat here. We can use it.

185
00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.650
[MOMONOSUKE]
That's ridiculous, Dogstorm!

186
00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:03.320
What're you saying?

187
00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:05.650
We'll delay the plan! We must!

188
00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:09.700
Alas, that is not
an option, my lord.

189
00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.080
Master Kin!

190
00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:20.420
Shinobu, stop this.

191
00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:25.420
We can't!
This is doomed to fail!

192
00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.140
[KIN'EMON]
And yet it must be done.

193
00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:30.850
You know this as well as I do.

194
00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:38.930
<b>Onigashima</b>

195
00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:39.860
[Orochi cackling]

196
00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:42.190
[KIN'EMON]
It must be tonight.

197
00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:47.660
[Orochi cackling]

198
00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.450
[NARRATOR]
The night before the festival,

199
00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:53.140
Orochi had already
thwarted their plans.

200
00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:56.950
<b>Two Days Ago</b>

201
00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:55.190
[NARRATOR]
Two days
before the Fire Festival,

202
00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.610
when hope still remained.

203
00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:59.450
<b>Amigasa 

Village</b>

204
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.800
Splendid. We now have
4,200 soldiers.

205
00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:07.890
I'm stunned. It's a miracle
that they have joined us!

206
00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.140
Attention, everyone!

207
00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:12.200
Thank you for all of
your hard work!

208
00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:12.430
Use the remaining time
for preparations and travel!

209
00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:16.310
Please use the remaining time
for preparations and travel!

210
00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:19.100
We'll meet at
the rendezvous port!

211
00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:20.480
Take care!

212
00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:24.650
[Soldiers cheer]

213
00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:28.390
<b>Itachi Port


Kuri</b>

214
00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:33.040
We gotta move 5,000 troops,
so get those ships in shape!

215
00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.160
[WORKERS]
Yessir!

216
00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:36.120
Perfect! You know
the rendezvous port,

217
00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:39.170
you know the time to be there,
can you dig it?

218
00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.670
No problem!
We'll see you there, for sure!

219
00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:42.880
Hell yeah!

220
00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:47.160
<b>Itachi

Port</b>
<b>Amigasa

Village</b>

221
00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.710
[USOPP]
Then, we'll split for now.

222
00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:47.180
We're meeting up with our
friends in Amigasa Village.

223
00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:48.260
On the day of the festival,

224
00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:50.600
we'll sail into battle
on the Sunny!

225
00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.430
The other boats are up to you!

226
00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:54.930
Got it! We'll work hard
and work fast!

227
00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.350
You taught us a lot.
You're awesome!

228
00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:58.400
Damn straight!

229
00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.940
Kaido won't even
know what hit him!

230
00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:04.820
Just two more days and
we're gonna kick some ass!

231
00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:09.280
[workers cheer]

232
00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:13.110
<b>Udon</b>

233
00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:10.860
[WORKER A]
We don't have enough timber!

234
00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:13.240
Cut up anything made of
wood that you can find!

235
00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:15.580
We can count on Ocho's
group to bring swords

236
00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:18.370
and other weapons
from Ringo. What's next?

237
00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:21.250
We'll put together some armor
from the enemies supplies!

238
00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.040
[WORKER C]
I don't know
if we can use these or not,

239
00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.760
but the factory here still has
a ton of heavy weapons

240
00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:27.090
they were going to sell.

241
00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:28.590
